 "text": "The rule's own exit nets +0.079R a trade in 2005-15 (month t +2.95) and +0.063R in 2016 → now (t +2.50). BE1: stop to entry once +1R reached: +0.057R / +0.057R net (t +2.25 / +2.37), max drawdown −51.6 / −27.3R against the rule's −42.2 / −33.8R. TR1: trail 1R behind the best price from +1R: +0.047R / +0.030R net (t +2.16 / +1.33), max drawdown −29.5 / −29.6R against the rule's −42.2 / −33.8R. PH1: half at +1R, rest to the rule's exit: +0.055R / +0.029R net (t +2.63 / +1.49), max drawdown −35.0 / −27.7R against the rule's −42.2 / −33.8R. About 34 % of trades reach +1R after their fill candle. The difference with the rule is the same before and after costs (the cost depends on entry and risk only). Control: on the random-entry placebo trades the same managements change little (median d BE1 +0.002, TR1 −0.003, PH1 −0.008), while on T1 each costs more than the placebo's 5-95 % band (BE1 −0.015, TR1 −0.033, PH1 −0.029): cutting or locking in at +1R takes away the days the breakout runs to 21:00, which is where its result comes from. TR1 and PH1 lower the drawdown a little; they also about halve the net R in 2016 → now. No management meets the pre-registered bar: the rule keeps its own exit (stop at the open, out at 21:00 UTC). Paper research; nothing live changes and no proposal is written.",
 "data": "OANDA mid M5 USD/JPY from the shared candle cache (edgekit), 2005-01-02 → 2026-11-19 (1651787 candles read); windows 2005-01-04 → 2015-12-31 and 2016-01-01 → 2026-11-19"
